<%--
Turnstile_Input

The Cloudflare Turnstile widget, as a form field. Drop it into any form whose endpoint calls
Rsx_Turnstile::validate() - above the submit button - and the transport is handled:

    <Turnstile_Input />

It renders a REAL hidden input named __turnstile, which is what makes one component work on
both transports with no app dependency: Rsx_Form.vals() sweeps hidden inputs, and a native
<form> POST serializes them. See Turnstile_Input.js for why this is not a Form_Input_Abstract.

TWO STATES, decided by whether the server exported a site key (window.rsxapp.turnstile):
  active   - Cloudflare renders its widget into the widget container; the hidden input starts
             empty and carries the token once the challenge resolves.
  inactive - an inert placeholder illustrates where the widget will sit, and the hidden input
             carries the sentinel 'inactive' that the server requires when the feature is off.

Args:
  $theme       auto | light | dark                        (default auto)
  $size        normal | flexible | compact                (default normal)
  $appearance  always | execute | interaction-only        (default always)

See: php artisan rsx:man turnstile
--%>
<Define:Turnstile_Input tag="div">
    <%
        // Both states are rendered; only one is shown. Deciding visibility HERE as well as in
        // on_render() is what stops the placeholder from flashing on an active page - on_render
        // then re-asserts it, idempotently, after every subsequent render.
        const _active = Turnstile.is_active();
        const _widget_style = _active ? '' : 'display:none;';
        const _placeholder_style = _active ? 'display:none;' : '';
    %>
    <input type="hidden" name="<%= Turnstile_Input.FIELD %>" $sid="token" />

    <div $sid="widget" class="Turnstile_Input__widget" style="<%= _widget_style %>"></div>

    <div $sid="placeholder" class="Turnstile_Input__placeholder" style="<%= _placeholder_style %>">
        <%-- Inline SVG, not an icon-font glyph: this is framework-core and the pages it is
             wired into (the login/portal auth screens) do not load the app theme's
             bootstrap-icons stylesheet, which would leave a blank square. --%>
        <svg class="Turnstile_Input__placeholder-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
             stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M8 1.2 14 3.4V8c0 3.2-2.4 5.6-6 6.8C4.4 13.6 2 11.2 2 8V3.4Z"></path>
            <path d="M5.4 8.1 7.2 9.9l3.5-3.6"></path>
        </svg>
        <span class="Turnstile_Input__placeholder-label">Human verification</span>
        <span class="Turnstile_Input__placeholder-note">(disabled)</span>
    </div>
</Define:Turnstile_Input>
